0..47 Comment "//! A rule term can bind a variable in a field."
48..51 Comment "//!"
52..127 Comment "//! A `pi+ (x : S) . T` port accepts `bind x . t`. The variable `x` has the"
128..185 Comment "//! representable sort `S`. Substitution instantiates it."
186..189 Comment "//!"
190..258 Comment "//! A `bind (a : N) . T` port abstracts atom `a`. A swap renames it."
259..333 Comment "//! A `Theory` value stores a field as a `Bind` node and its variable as a"
334..411 Comment "//! `Bvar` node. It stores an abstraction as an `Abs` node and its atom as an"
412..478 Comment "//! `Occ` node. A program distinguishes the two binders by `case`."
479..482 Comment "//!"
483..584 Comment "//! - cites: [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]"
585..588 Comment "//!"
589..788 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]: https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10 \"Kaposi and Xie, Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories\""
790..868 Comment "/// No process outside the restriction can use the channel `c` of `listen`, so"
869..945 Comment "/// the restricted receive never fires. The checker orients the law, and the"
946..977 Comment "/// kernel replays its verdict."
